  "raw_text": "202\n\nRayaka bara Smalkaia aidrubanka tâ brabrira\n \n–\n \nLife and Ministry Meeting Overseer\n \n/ Superintendente de la\nreunión Vida y Ministerio\n\nRayaka yabaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto give life\n \n/ dar vida\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nlv-8\n):\n \nGâd kupia l\nȃ\nka daukaia dukyara selp rayakam yabram\n \n–\n \nYou gave your own life in order to do God’s will\n \n/\nDiste tu propia vida para hacer la voluntad de Dios)\n\nJehova ra rayaka yabaia bara tahbi daukan lâka briaia ba\n \n–\n \nD\nedication and baptism\n \n/\n \nLa dedicación y el\n\nbautismo\n\nWan rayaka yabaia\n \n–\n \nto give our life, to dedicate our life\n \n/ dar nuestra vida, dedicar nuestra vida\n\nWan rayaka\n \n(G\nâ\nd ra)\n \nyabaia ba\n \n–\n \nour dedication, the dedication of our life\n \n/ nuestra dedicación, la\n\ndedicación de nuestra vida\n\nSilp ai rayaka ra\n \n–\n \nin their/his/her/its own life\n \n/ en su propia vida\n\nUpla\n \nrayaka\n \n–\n \nhuman life\n \n/\n \nvida humana\n\n(Ex/Ej\n(\nmwb\n-\n08/20\n):\n \nUpla rayaka ba Gâd kulki ba baku yawan kulkpi\n \n–\n \nRespect human life like God respects human life\n \n/\n\nRespeta la vida humana como Dios respeta\n \nla vida humana\n)\n\nUpla\n \nrayaka\n \nra takan\n \nstur\nka\n \n(a/t:\n \nU\npla rayaka sturka\n)\n \n–\n \nlife\n-\nstory, experience in a person’s life\n, interview\n \n/\n\nhistoria de vida, experiencia en la vida de una persona\n, entrevista\n\nRayakas\n \n(adj)\n \n–\n \nlifeless\n \n/ sin vida\n\nRayapisa\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nwatermelon\n \n/ sandía\n\nRent munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto rent\n \n/\n \nrentar,\n \nalquilar,\n \nar\nren\nd\nar\n\n(\nEx/Ej:\n \nWitin utla kum rent munan\n \n–\n \nHe rented a house\n \n/ Alquiló una casa\n)\n\nReveleshan\n \n(a/t:\n \nParam Marikan\n)\n \n–\n \nRevelation\n \n(Bible book) / Apocalipsis (libro bíblico)\n\nRid munaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto read\n \n/ leer\n \n(See also/ Ver también:\n \nAisi kaikaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto read\n \n/ leer)\n\nRidi\n \n(a/t:\n \nRedi\n) (adj)\n \n–\n \nready, prepared\n \n/ listo, preparado\n\nRidi daukaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nRedi daukaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto prepare, to make ready\n \n/ preparar\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth4\n):\n \nAisanka kum ridi daukisma taim, ...\n \n–\n \nWhen you are preparing a talk, ...\n \n/ Cuando estás preparando un\ndsiscurso, ...)\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nth-4\n):\n \nBaibil tikska kum kau aisi kaikras kainara, wali nani kupia ba ridi dauks.\n \n–\n \nBefore reading a Bible text, make\n\nyour listeners’ hearts ready.\n \n/ Antes de leer un texto bíblico, prepare los corazones de sus oyentes.)\n\nRidi daukri ba\n \n(\ndb\n-\nJ\nirimaya\n \n18:8,10\n)\n \n–\n \nwhat I was ready to do, what I intended to do\n \n/ Lo que estaba listo\n\npara hacer, lo que tenía la intención de hacer\n\nRidi kaia sa\n \n–\n \nwe/he/she must be ready\n \n/ nosotros/él/ella debe estar listo\n\nRidi munaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nRedi munaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto prepare, to make ready, to cause to get ready\n \n/ prepararse, hacer\nprepararse\n\n(Ex/Ej(\nmwb-12/18\n):\n \nwahma nani ra ridi muns\n \n–\n \nget young men ready; train young men\n \n/ prepara a los hombres jóvenes;\nentrenar a hombres jóvenes)\n\nRidi takaia\n \n(a/t:\n \nRedi takaia\n) (v)\n \n–\n \nto become prepared, to come to be prepared, to get ready\n \n/ estar preparado,\nvenir a estar preparado, prepararse\n\nPain ridi takaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto prepare well\n \n/ prepararse bien\n\nRidi\n \ntakaia wauhkataya\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nworkbook\n \n/ libro de trabajo\n\nRidi takanka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npreparation\n \n/ preparaci\nó\nn\n\nRidi takan l\nâ\nka\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \npreparedness,\n \nreadiness,\n \npreparation\n \n/ preparaci\nó\nn\n, disposición\n\nRih\n \n(n/s)\n \n–\n \nfever\n \n/\n \nfiebre\n\nRih\n \ndaukaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have a fever, to be affected by a fever\n \n/ tener fiebre, ser afectado por una fiebre\n\nRih ai daukisa\n \n–\n \nfever affects me, I have a fever\n \n/ la fiebre me afecta, tengo fiebre\n\nRih mai daukisa\n \n–\n \nfever affects you, you have a fever\n \n/ la fiebre te afecta, tienes fiebre\n\nRihka\n \n(\nn\n/s\n-\nconstruct\n)\n \n–\n \nfever\n \n/ fiebre\n\nRihka ai/mai alkan\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \n(1p/2p)\n \nto be caught by a fever\n \n/ coger una fiebre\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nRihka ai alkan\n \n–\n \nA fever caught me\n \n/ Me dió fiebre)\n\nRihka alkaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto catch a fever\n \n/ tener fiebre\n\nRihka ai alkan\n \n–\n \nI caught a fever\n \n/ tengo fiebre\n\nRihka mai alkan\n \n–\n \nyou caught a fever\n \n/ tienes fiebre\n\nRihka briaia\n \n(v)\n \n–\n \nto have a fever\n \n/ tener fiebre\n\n(Ex/Ej:\n \nWitin rihka brisa\n \n–\n \nHe has a fever\n \n/ El\n \ntiene fiebre\n)",
